  [1m4. Data flow[0m

  Login: submit → [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m → [38;5;153mauth.login[39m → on success, [38;5;153midentity.setIdentity(record)[39m → one attribution log line
  carrying [38;5;153muserId[39m and [38;5;153musername[39m. Any other form imports [38;5;153midentity.js[39m and calls [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m; it never touches [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m
  directly.

  Logout: button → [38;5;153midentity.clearIdentity()[39m → storage key removed. This is the shared-machine escape hatch I flagged
  earlier.

  [1m5. Error handling[0m

  [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m throws in Safari private mode, when quota is exhausted, and when site data is disabled. Since this is
  attribution-only, [1ma storage failure must never break logging in[0m: reads and writes are wrapped, a failure falls back to
  an in-memory store for the page's lifetime, and it warns once. Corrupt JSON under the key is treated as "no identity"
  and the key is cleared. A failed login writes nothing and leaves any existing identity untouched.

  [1m6. Testing[0m

  [38;5;153mnode --test[39m (built in, zero dependencies), tests in [38;5;153mtest/identity.test.js[39m, driven through
  [38;5;153mcreateIdentityStore(fakeStorage)[39m with a [38;5;153mMap[39m-backed fake — so they cover set/get/clear, the corrupt-JSON path, and the
  throwing-storage fallback without a browser.

  This needs [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m, which would break the existing CommonJS [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m.
  Rather than edit those unrelated files, I'll add a one-line [38;5;153msrc/package.json[39m containing [38;5;153m{"type": "commonjs"}[39m — they
  keep working untouched.

  [1m7. Out of scope[0m

  No gating or authorization, no auth token, no real network call, no multi-user switching, no analytics backend
  (attribution goes to [38;5;153mconsole[39m for now).

  If this looks right, say so and I'll write it up as a spec at
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-17-user-identity-design.md[39m for your review before any code gets written.

